From ec6466159a3aa32f25aa72c30fc433c74b98fe3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Catrysse <jan.catrysse@geoxyz.eu>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:25:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the maximum number of custom query blocks on My page
 configurable (#27313).

My page allows at most three issuequery blocks, as a constant in
Redmine::MyPage::CORE_BLOCKS since r16413 (#1565). How many issue lists a
dashboard can carry depends on the size of the queries, on how many users
open the page and on the server, which is a judgement for an administrator
rather than a number in the source. Today it cannot be moved in either
direction: an installation whose users want more cannot allow them, and one
that has been hurt by heavy dashboard queries cannot ask for fewer.

:max_occurs may now name a setting instead of holding an integer, and
MyPage.max_occurs resolves it, clamped to a minimum of one so that a blank
or zero value cannot disable a block type a user already has on the page. An
integer still means what it did, so a block declaring a plain :max_occurs is
unaffected. The default of the new my_page_max_issuequery_blocks setting is
3, so nothing changes for an existing installation until an administrator
moves it -- note-9 on #27313 asks for content to load asynchronously before
the number of queries is raised, and this raises nothing.

Lowering the setting below what a user already has does not remove or hide
their blocks: block_options only decides whether another one may be added,
so the existing blocks keep rendering.
---
 config/locales/de.yml | 1 +
 config/locales/es.yml | 1 +
 config/locales/fr.yml | 1 +
 config/locales/nl.yml | 1 +
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

